WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.760
The first film followed repair while one strand still held a usable partner.

2
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:08.360
What can a cell do when a break cuts both strands?

3
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:12.500
The blue chromosome now separates into two ends.

4
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.960
No continuous partner crosses the gap.

5
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.080
The cell can work with those ends, or search for matching DNA elsewhere.

6
00:00:24.583 --> 00:00:28.863
A broken chromosome can join its ends or copy a matching template.

7
00:00:30.143 --> 00:00:33.863
Non-homologous end joining chooses the ends already present.

8
00:00:35.303 --> 00:00:40.483
Homologous recombination copies a matching template, usually the sister chromatid.

9
00:00:41.823 --> 00:00:43.743
Neither name guarantees one outcome.

10
00:00:44.943 --> 00:00:49.143
The ends' condition and the available template shape what happens next.

11
00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:51.583
Start with end joining.

12
00:00:53.023 --> 00:00:57.423
Teal Ku rings grip both blue ends and recruit partners that hold them together.

13
00:00:58.763 --> 00:01:02.683
Clean, compatible ends may be joined without changing their sequence.

14
00:01:04.143 --> 00:01:07.503
Ends that do not fit need trimming or filling before ligation.

15
00:01:08.863 --> 00:01:13.683
That processing can remove or add bases, so accuracy depends on the break.

16
00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:17.327
End joining needs no matching template.

17
00:01:18.587 --> 00:01:20.907
It can therefore operate throughout the cell cycle.

18
00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:26.987
Before DNA replication, that matters because no sister chromatid exists.

19
00:01:28.307 --> 00:01:32.247
After replication, another option becomes available beside it.

20
00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:36.830
Here are two cells, one before replication and one after.

21
00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:40.270
Which cell can copy from a sister chromatid?

22
00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:44.610
Watch where you expect a matching gold chromosome to appear.

23
00:01:50.617 --> 00:01:54.577
After replication, each chromosome has a sister chromatid.

24
00:01:55.737 --> 00:02:01.057
That matching copy makes homologous recombination useful during and after

25
00:02:01.057 --> 00:02:06.597
replication. The broken blue chromosome aligns beside the gold sister.

26
00:02:07.877 --> 00:02:12.757
Before replication, the sister is absent, so this sister-templated route is

27
00:02:12.757 --> 00:02:13.757
unavailable.

28
00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:19.670
Homologous recombination first reshapes the break into single-stranded tails.

29
00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:24.590
A recombinase coats a tail and helps it search the gold sister.

30
00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.090
At matching DNA, the tail invades.

31
00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:34.270
Its end primes new green DNA, copying information from the intact template.

32
00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:39.190
The repaired chromosome keeps the sister's sequence across the gap.

33
00:02:40.233 --> 00:02:42.293
Copying does not force a crossover.

34
00:02:43.753 --> 00:02:48.313
Often the extended strand leaves the donor and pairs with the other broken end.

35
00:02:49.533 --> 00:02:53.013
Another branch can form crossed junctions before separation.

36
00:02:54.413 --> 00:02:57.313
Both begin by using matching DNA as information.

37
00:02:58.517 --> 00:02:59.957
Reset the same break.

38
00:03:01.477 --> 00:03:05.837
End joining preserves clean compatible ends, but processing may change them.

39
00:03:07.157 --> 00:03:12.337
Homologous recombination can restore missing sequence from a sister, but only when

40
00:03:12.337 --> 00:03:13.517
that template exists.

41
00:03:14.697 --> 00:03:17.937
The choice is not a contest between bad and good repair.

42
00:03:19.097 --> 00:03:22.997
It responds to available information and cell-cycle context.

43
00:03:24.117 --> 00:03:26.617
When both strands break, ask what remains.

44
00:03:28.057 --> 00:03:30.677
Are two joinable ends the only local evidence?

45
00:03:31.897 --> 00:03:33.957
Is an intact sister nearby to copy?

46
00:03:35.277 --> 00:03:38.477
Those questions predict the route and its possible outcome.
